INT. CHEESE AFFINAGE CAVE - NIGHT

Damp limestone. Shelves of waxed wheels stretch back into the dark. A single lantern on a hook. Cool, quiet, almost holy.

A long oak table at the center. Five people sit around it with tasting knives and small plates, like it's a dinner party.

At the head, ARNAUD DELACROIX-MBALLA (60s, owner, white apron). He cuts a wedge, offers it round. Steady hands.

To his right, SABINE QUIRK (30s, buyer, scarf). She takes the wedge. Doesn't eat it.

Across from her, YOSEF ABRAMOWITZ (50s, inspector). He chews slowly, eyes on the ceiling.

Beside him, LEILANI KEAWE (20s, sommelier). She pours wine. Pours a little too much into one glass.

At the foot, TOMAS ESPINOZA-REID (40s, silent partner), jacket on, buttoned.

ARNAUD
Eighteen months. Raw milk.

SABINE
It's lovely.

ARNAUD
You haven't tasted it.

She lifts it. Eats. Smiles with her mouth only.

YOSEF
Earthy.

LEILANI
A little mushroom. Hazelnut at the finish.

TOMAS
It's fine.

Arnaud nods. Cuts another wedge. Sets it before Tomas. Tomas does not touch it.

ARNAUD
You're not hungry?

TOMAS
I ate.

ARNAUD
Before you came?

TOMAS
Before.

Sabine sets down her knife. Gently. Parallel to the plate.

Leilani refills Yosef's glass. His hand covers it too late. She keeps pouring anyway.

YOSEF
That's plenty.

LEILANI
Is it?

She holds his gaze. He lowers his hand.

ARNAUD
(to the room)
Strange thing, an affinage cave. Everything in here changes. Slowly. If you do nothing, it turns.

SABINE
Turns into what?

ARNAUD
Whatever it was always going to be.

Silence. Water drips somewhere in the dark. Tomas shifts. His jacket pulls open an inch. A holster, dull black. He buttons it again.

Nobody looks at it. Everybody saw it.

Arnaud sets down his own knife. Folds his hands. Smiles at the table like a man who has just finished a long meal.

ARNAUD (CONT'D)
Now. Shall we discuss the shipment?
